{
  "_id": "bdaf020fcade8e21",
  "name": "Shapeshifter",
  "type": "npc",
  "img": "systems/sr2e/assets/creature_portraits/shapeshifter.webp",
  "system": {
    "biography": "<p>An animal that takes metahuman form. The sheet's printed block is the human form; its animal form is under <strong>Forms</strong>. Six common species are set up (Bear, Fox, Leopard, Seal, Tiger, Wolf): keep the one your shapeshifter is and delete the other five forms and their Natural Attacks.</p><p><strong>Animal form</strong> (core p.234): the animal's attributes (A, core p.233 — the large specimen where the table offers one, per p.230) with Body A + 2, Quickness A + 1, Strength A + 2, Charisma 5, Intelligence 3, Willpower 3, Essence (8), Reaction 5*, attack (A + 1)(A). Only the form's natural attack works in animal form; the Unarmed Strike and any gear stay with the human form.</p><p><strong>Powers:</strong> Enhanced Physical Attributes (in animal form), Regeneration</p><p><strong>Weaknesses:</strong> Allergy (Silver, Severe), Vulnerability (Silver)</p><p>Shapeshifter is on: Regeneration (wounds vanish at the start of the next Combat Turn; a death check when it goes down), Allergy + Vulnerability to silver in damage resistance, dual-natured.</p><p><em>Running multiplier: human ×5; animal = the animal's + 1 (Bear ×4, Fox ×5, Leopard ×5, Seal ×5 in water and ×3 on land, Tiger ×5, Wolf ×5) — the sheet uses ×3, apply by hand. Perception: the animal's (human form 3). Bear form keeps the bear's natural armor 2. Stats: SR2E p.234; species p.230.</em></p>",
